# A blind reviewer (a fresh agent given only the review bundle) found what the checks cannot.
# Its findings, pinned where it pointed:
note 10,16 5x5 "hooked dark-grey glyph on the stem reads as a letter or scratch; remove it"
note 9,7 7x3 "the two lichen dashes pair up into a face; make the spots deliberate, of varied size"
note 3,4 18x10 "the cap is dark and close in value to the grass, and nothing marks it as a glowcap"
# The crack goes; the stem stays lit from the left.
rect 10,16 4x4 c=stone4 fill
# The cap in the props' wood ramp, lighter and warmer than the grass, tone for tone.
fill 20,9 c=wood1 mode=global
fill 4,8 c=wood2 mode=global
fill 3,8 c=wood3 mode=global
line 7,13 16,13 c=wood0
line 8,14 15,14 c=wood0
# Spots that glow, in brass: three sizes, none paired.
px 9,7 10,7 c=wood3
px 14,9 15,9 c=wood2
px 12,7 13,7 12,8 13,8 c=brass2
px 7,10 8,10 c=brass1
px 17,8 17,9 c=brass1
note done n1
note done n2
note done n3
